1
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:05,580
The End Ow... Ugh...

2
00:00:06,160 --> 00:00:06,990
Hmm...

3
00:00:07,073 --> 00:00:08,417
You should really have a
doctor take a look at that.

4
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:10,037
Yeah, yeah, I already know that...

5
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:12,697
But I want you to give me a bit
of first aid in the meantime.

6
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:14,074
Alright, take it easy.

7
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:17,024
Wait, Fugo, you're not gonna...

8
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:18,270
AHHHHH!

9
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:22,377
Have you lost your mind?

10
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:23,695
Did that just happen?

11
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:27,077
Holy shit, you sealed him
up like a freaking manga.

12
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:30,457
Hey, Narancia, you mind grabbing the
duct tape and wrapping up his midsection?

13
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:31,370
I'm on it.

14
00:00:31,453 --> 00:00:34,157
This hack job isn't going
to get infected, is it?

15
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:35,887
Don't worry, you'll be fine.

16
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:37,797
It's actually kind of growing on me.

17
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:38,762
May I chime in?

18
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:42,920
Vagazzi, you've made me proud.

19
00:00:43,860 --> 00:00:47,697
It's thanks to all of your efforts
that we made it to Capri alive.

20
00:00:47,780 --> 00:00:52,097
Our would-be attackers have been neutralized
and are being held on the ship for now.

21
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:53,945
The obstacle has been cleared.

22
00:00:54,140 --> 00:00:54,980
Then let's go!

23
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:56,537
There's no time like the present!

24
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:58,738
Our 10 billion lira treasure awaits!

25
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:00,141
Enough suspense.

26
00:01:00,420 --> 00:01:01,357
Where'd you hide it?

27
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:03,460
A hidden safe at the bank? No.

28
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:06,800
You must have buried it in
some cave on the island.

29
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:09,799
I need you to wait a little longer.

30
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:12,197
Where's this coming from?

31
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,280
And why do we need to wait around?

32
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:16,230
Shh!

33
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:19,940
Could you wait a few?

34
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:22,497
There are still some people left in there.

35
00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:25,227
Well, think you could
clean this place later?

36
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:28,760
So you must be La Toilette?

37
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:30,390
Huh?

38
00:01:30,473 --> 00:01:31,351
What do you mean by that?

39
00:01:32,620 --> 00:01:37,444
If your name was La Toilette, that'd make
this place your house, giving you a say.

40
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:40,537
After all, one calls the
shots in their own home.

41
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:41,450
Of course,

42
00:01:41,533 --> 00:01:43,460
if this isn't actually your house,

43
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:45,837
then you really have no
business ordering me around.

44
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:46,750
What?

45
00:01:46,833 --> 00:01:48,100
Hold it, moron!

46
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:51,342
What part of comeback
later don't you understand?

47
00:01:56,180 --> 00:01:57,280
The hell?

48
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:59,577
Hey, what do you think you're doing, pal?

49
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:00,490
Knock it off!

50
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:02,480
What the hell, user?

51
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:05,200
Come on, I'll slice you apart! Wait!

52
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:07,457
Back off now, Narancia.

53
00:02:07,540 --> 00:02:08,517
But I want to cut this fool!

54
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:10,188
Things aren't as they seem.

55
00:02:10,620 --> 00:02:11,450
Huh?

56
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:13,320
That stern voice.

57
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:15,360
We've kept you waiting.

58
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:18,200
Gentlemen, bow your heads.

59
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:20,140
This is Mr.

60
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:22,340
Pericolo, a Cape from Passione.

61
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:27,446
I've come all the way here for
the 10 billion lira, Bucciarati.

62
00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:37,957
I'll see you

63
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:45,040
next

64
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:46,070
time.

65
00:03:46,153 --> 00:03:49,020
Fukatu no tamashi Dish yo?

66
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:55,500
Fighting cold!

67
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:19,537
I was the one who requested your
team travel here in the first place.

68
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:21,300
Please, everyone at ease.

69
00:04:22,380 --> 00:04:24,340
You must be the rookie, huh?

70
00:04:25,020 --> 00:04:25,850
Si.

71
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:28,060
Bucerates told me all about you.

72
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:32,057
You are with Passione now, which
makes you part of the Family.

73
00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:36,360
I know we've only just met, but
by all means call me Mr. Pericolo.

74
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:38,100
I appreciate that, sir.

75
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:42,940
Oh, Sunny, pardon the
rough reception earlier.

76
00:04:43,640 --> 00:04:47,052
She hates it when people touch
her without her permission.

77
00:04:47,180 --> 00:04:48,010
Whatever.

78
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:49,550
Not cool!

79
00:04:49,633 --> 00:04:51,380
It's yes, sir! Mr. Periculum.

80
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,220
If I may, why the elaborate disguise?

81
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:58,140
Oh, I have my reasons,
but I'll clarify later.

82
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:01,605
Before that, are you
positive that you have it?

83
00:05:01,860 --> 00:05:05,100
The 10 billion lira
contribution to the Family?

84
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:06,950
Indeed.

85
00:05:07,033 --> 00:05:07,920
Right here, in fact.

86
00:05:08,580 --> 00:05:09,720
Back it up a bit!

87
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:10,897
What did you just say?

88
00:05:10,980 --> 00:05:12,740
He said it's here! But where?

89
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:16,175
You're gonna have to be more specific.

90
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:18,761
Sorry, but all I see are urinals.

91
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:24,157
Whoa! What?

92
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:25,769
You hid it inside of that?

93
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:28,577
Well, I can't deny it was
secure, but holy moly,

94
00:05:28,660 --> 00:05:31,307
if those guys knew what
they were pissing on!

95
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:33,920
Hmm, it's authentic.

96
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:38,719
This necklace alone is worth at
least seven or eight hundred million.

97
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:44,620
Bucciarati, I won't badger you for details
on how you obtain this cash of riches.

98
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:47,437
The Family cares not about your methods,

99
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:49,997
only that you follow
through with the funds.

100
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:50,910
Wait, hang on!

101
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,197
You're putting it away already?

102
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:53,717
Could I touch it a little?

103
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:55,260
I'd settle for a whiff!

104
00:05:57,060 --> 00:06:00,877
This treasure is proof
incarnate that the man standing

105
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:04,440
before us today is one of
tremendous intellect and faith.

106
00:06:05,380 --> 00:06:08,040
Well done, Bucciarati. You did it.

107
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:11,180
I hereby promote you to the rank of Cape.

108
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:13,860
Hey, did you hear that? He did it!

109
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:17,260
After all that,
Bucciarati's finally a Cape!

110
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:20,640
Since Polpo is no longer among the living,

111
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:24,237
you are now the successor to
the entirety of his territory.

112
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:28,000
You'll oversee all interests
related to the Family in Napoli,

113
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:30,085
including gambling, extortion,

114
00:06:30,380 --> 00:06:33,498
port contraband, and restaurant
and hotel operations.

115
00:06:34,140 --> 00:06:36,540
50 % goes to the Family.

116
00:06:36,860 --> 00:06:38,820
The rest is yours for the taking.

117
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:41,630
Incredible!

118
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:43,700
So much power just like that!

119
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:49,040
With Bucciarati's smarts and charisma, our
little gang is gonna be rolling in dough!

120
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:50,910
Man,

121
00:06:50,993 --> 00:06:52,297
it's like everything
started being set into

122
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:54,940
motion once that new guy Giorno got here.

123
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:57,280
He's a crazy good luck charm!

124
00:06:57,520 --> 00:06:59,257
Oh, and there's one more thing.

125
00:06:59,340 --> 00:07:04,197
I know you haven't had time to digest
your new duties as Polpo's successor.

126
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:08,120
But you should know he still
had one job left unfinished.

127
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:12,957
Naturally this responsibility
will now rest on your shoulders.

128
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:15,628
Are you willing to
accept his final mission?

129
00:07:15,940 --> 00:07:17,897
It'll be a heavy burden to bear.

130
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:20,200
So I'm to finish what he started.

131
00:07:21,660 --> 00:07:24,900
Be aware this is a direct
order from the boss.

132
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:26,780
The boss?

133
00:07:27,140 --> 00:07:28,597
I see. Unreal.

134
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:32,000
Isn't this the same boss no
one's ever met in person?

135
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:34,677
And now we're getting
an order right from him?

136
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:35,590
That's right.

137
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:37,840
I'll deliver his words myself.

138
00:07:39,720 --> 00:07:42,602
Your mission is to safeguard
the boss's daughter.

139
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:45,957
Laying down your lives if needed.

140
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:46,922
End of message.

141
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:49,460
His daughter? The boss?

142
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:50,617
Did he say daughter?

143
00:07:50,700 --> 00:07:55,112
The daughter of the boss we were planning
on tracking down and eliminating?

144
00:07:55,320 --> 00:07:58,160
Your safeguarding obligations begin now.

145
00:07:58,420 --> 00:08:00,020
I'm turning her over to you

146
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:02,760
Turning her over.

147
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:04,510
Bucciarati.

148
00:08:04,900 --> 00:08:06,320
Could that guy be?

149
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:08,800
No that woman.

150
00:08:09,540 --> 00:08:12,040
She must be the boss's daughter.

151
00:08:12,900 --> 00:08:16,440
Could that really be her I have to

152
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:19,320
Well, you know, that's fine.

153
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:20,360
Go ahead Trish

154
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:26,217
For now, stay by her side.

155
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:28,160
She is now our priority.

156
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:30,630
Bucciarati?

157
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:36,700
Her name is Trish Una,
and she's 15 years old.

158
00:08:37,180 --> 00:08:41,700
The name Una comes from her mother, so
it has no association with the boss.

159
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:46,553
Trish has also never met the boss, so
she doesn't know anything about him.

160
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:51,640
Bucciarati, as you know, no one has
knowledge of the boss's true identity.

161
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:55,500
But of course, even someone
like the boss has a past.

162
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:57,980
His youth is especially intriguing.

163
00:08:58,980 --> 00:09:02,960
Two months ago, in a hospital
in a small town in Calabria,

164
00:09:03,300 --> 00:09:06,440
a woman named Donatella
succumbed to illness.

165
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,960
Just days before her death,

166
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:14,440
she initiated a frantic search
for a man named Solidonazo.

167
00:09:15,140 --> 00:09:18,460
The man she was looking
for was Trish's father.

168
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:21,417
I assume it was a final act of love for a

169
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:24,317
daughter who'd soon be
left to fend for herself,

170
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:25,237
but...

171
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:28,085
She couldn't find him
because he doesn't exist.

172
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:33,140
It was just an alias, used by the boss in
his youth to conceal his true identity.

173
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:34,470
Am I right?

174
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:39,180
But he who seeks Naso
must exercise caution.

175
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:44,900
Anyone with any standing whatsoever in
Passione knows to take these words to heart.

176
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:50,260
To peer into the depths of the boss's
past is to defy the Family itself.

177
00:09:51,380 --> 00:09:54,100
Word of Donatella spread like wildfire.

178
00:09:54,380 --> 00:09:58,200
As you can imagine, with news
of a daughter, rumors exploded.

179
00:09:58,540 --> 00:10:01,128
Of course, the hearsay
reached the boss too.

180
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:04,860
His resolution was unsurprisingly swift.

181
00:10:05,180 --> 00:10:08,780
By way of several intermediaries,
he extended his order.

182
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:13,257
Upon Donatella's death, I
was to become her guardian.

183
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:15,700
He must have known instinctively.

184
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:20,275
He lived his life without
knowing she had ever existed,

185
00:10:20,380 --> 00:10:23,680
yet suddenly he knew Trish was his own

186
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:25,950
flesh and blood.

187
00:10:26,033 --> 00:10:28,620
Shortly after taking
Trish into my custody,

188
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:33,577
I discovered someone was attempting to hunt
her down and take the girl out for good.

189
00:10:33,660 --> 00:10:36,960
Had the directive arrived
30 minutes later, I've no

190
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:41,037
doubt Trish's pursuers
would have taken her away.

191
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:43,140
They would have surely killed her.

192
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:44,680
But who'd do this?

193
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:46,837
Who would want to kill
the boss's daughter?

194
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:48,979
Traitors to the Family, of course.

195
00:10:49,120 --> 00:10:51,557
And there's no telling how many there are.

196
00:10:51,640 --> 00:10:53,677
They are attempting to
overthrow the boss and

197
00:10:53,760 --> 00:10:56,337
take control of all the
drug trafficking routes.

198
00:10:56,420 --> 00:10:57,250
Drugs again.

199
00:10:57,600 --> 00:11:02,760
These idiotas have convinced themselves the
girl possesses secret intel on the boss.

200
00:11:02,980 --> 00:11:05,804
They want intelligence
on how to topple the boss

201
00:11:06,220 --> 00:11:07,497
when they carry out their coup.

202
00:11:07,580 --> 00:11:09,540
But she has no such knowledge.

203
00:11:09,820 --> 00:11:11,580
Trish is a vulnerable teen

204
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:13,560
in a strange new life.

205
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:15,500
How long will we protect her?

206
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:16,677
About seven days.

207
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:19,217
And likely it'll be
even shorter than that.

208
00:11:19,300 --> 00:11:23,124
You'll be relieved of duty once
the boss eliminates the traitors.

209
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:27,360
Leave this island immediately
and place her under concealment.

210
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:29,420
This arrangement is top secret.

211
00:11:29,700 --> 00:11:31,960
Only the boss and I know of it. Mr.

212
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:36,100
Pericolo, to clarify, this
mission was first Polpo's.

213
00:11:36,420 --> 00:11:37,949
Isn't that right, Signore?

214
00:11:38,080 --> 00:11:39,577
Which means...

215
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:41,760
That our enemies are stand-users.

216
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:45,500
I'd say that is a good guess, my boy.

217
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:50,000
In all likelihood they'll
be working in teams as well.

218
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:53,379
Unfortunately, we don't yet
know how many there are.

219
00:11:53,560 --> 00:11:55,240
I don't possess a stand.

220
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:58,227
I've now done everything
I can to assist you.

221
00:11:58,660 --> 00:12:02,040
If I obtain further intel,
I'll find a way to reach you.

222
00:12:17,940 --> 00:12:19,320
Do you need something?

223
00:12:20,560 --> 00:12:21,390
Yeah, uh,

224
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:27,080
will you be, well, um, are you the group
that'll be escorting me from here on out?

225
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:30,497
Yes, that is correct.

226
00:12:30,580 --> 00:12:32,815
The six of us are here for you, Trish.

227
00:12:33,140 --> 00:12:36,493
While you're with us, we will
protect you with our lives.

228
00:12:37,300 --> 00:12:38,130
I see.

229
00:12:38,213 --> 00:12:39,098
Then do me a favor.

230
00:12:39,580 --> 00:12:42,874
Could you please take off
your jacket for just a minute?

231
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:44,797
You want me to take off my jacket?

232
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:45,710
But what for?

233
00:12:45,793 --> 00:12:46,897
Don't worry, just take it off.

234
00:12:46,980 --> 00:12:50,627
Trust me, I have no interest in
seeing you devoid of clothing!

235
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:52,753
You've made that clear.

236
00:12:56,700 --> 00:12:58,777
I'm out of handkerchiefs,
so go buy me one.

237
00:12:58,860 --> 00:13:02,780
While you're at it, get more nylons
and Givenchy blush number two.

238
00:13:03,420 --> 00:13:06,697
Oh, and those nylons better be the
ones with the garter at the thigh.

239
00:13:06,780 --> 00:13:08,920
And grab a copy of Vogitalia.

240
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:10,857
Mineral water would be nice too.

241
00:13:10,940 --> 00:13:12,940
But it has to be from France.

242
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:15,837
I'd rather keel over than
drink that other stuff.

243
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:19,567
When you're done ogling the
scenery, get started on that list.

244
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:25,615
Protect the daughter of the boss, huh?

245
00:13:26,820 --> 00:13:29,137
One minute we're hunting the bastard down,

246
00:13:29,220 --> 00:13:32,573
and the next we're face to
face with his flesh and blood.

247
00:13:33,820 --> 00:13:35,757
Still, this has to be done.

248
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:38,180
If we really follow through on this,

249
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:42,017
the boss will give Bucciarati the
same kind of trust he gave Polpo.

250
00:13:42,100 --> 00:13:45,400
But if we fail, our story won't end well.

251
00:13:45,820 --> 00:13:50,160
Everyone aboard this ship is
aware of that cruel reality.

252
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:54,520
What's with you?

253
00:13:54,860 --> 00:13:56,272
Chill out, sweetie baby.

254
00:13:56,580 --> 00:13:58,815
I'm just trying to show you some love.

255
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:01,680
Hey, come on.

256
